            "@id": "ihh:LAM-S-0009"
          },
          "ihh:quote": "Lamarr and Antheil's frequency hopping reduced the risk of detection or jamming of radio-controlled torpedoes. Multiple radio frequencies were used to broadcast a radio signal, switching frequencies at split-second intervals in a seemingly random manner that would sound like mere noise to anyone listening.",
          "ihh:locator": "paragraph 2"
        }
