      "ihh:notes": "Artifacts research 2026-10-20: 9 page images dn1929-d-242-00668..00676.jpg (catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/DN1929_PropertyControlBranch_USACA/DN1929_0242/images/), page 2 is 2980x3570 px. Rights from the holder's useRestriction.status in the record snapshot. Pages: 1 file cover; 2 USFA Property Control Branch memo 7 January 1946; 3-4 Paul Reiner letter December 7th 1945; 5 reply 7 January 1946; 6 cover letter 24 January 1946; 7-9 British Element ACA letter 12 Jan 46. Stop 1 (Vienna).\nAuthorship set on 2026-10-20: private (Paul Reiner, British Element, Allied Commission for Austria, USFA Property Control Branch) (private-writings rule, DECISIONS 2026-10-20): M-92 property file with private and non-U.S. correspondence.\nApplied the approved rights rule (DECISIONS 2026-10-20, private writings in public archives, private-writings rule) on 2026-10-20: license_class set back to unknown (link-only): private writing; no sourced death year for Paul Reiner; the holder's statement 'Unrestricted' alone is not a rights grant for a private writing.\nEdit lock (2026-10-20): rights fields changed after verification; adversary verdict 'supported' by codex:gpt-6.1-sol (run adv-20261020T165440-9590, 2026-10-20) cleared for re-verification.\nAuthorship set on 2026-10-20: private (Paul Reiner, Walker M. Treece, John G. Arnold, Director, Finance Division, British Element, Allied Commission for Austria (signature unreadable)) (private-writings rule, DECISIONS 2026-10-20): adversary 2026-10-20: list every named signer."
