      "ihh:notes": "Round 9 records (research R9-M-LAM-001, 2026-10-29). Chapter: lamarr/birth. Shows: The item headed \"Hedy Lamarr a Citizen\" in its column; OCR: \"Hedwig Eva Maria Kiesler, better known as Hedy Lamarr, actress, gets her American citizenship today. Miss Lamarr, 38, who came here in 1937 from her native Vienna\" Holder date: 1953-04-10. Resolution: crop region 700,4100,1900,1500 of the page (IIIF https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_carmen_ver01:data:sn83045462:00280606145:1953041001:0642/700,4100,1900,1500/full/0/default.jpg). Preview previews/lam-birth-evestar-1953-04-10-p6.jpg sha256 89510017b7a1b1ebc2aefc2bdd7a259c1e5c162112d556f91966e1c5a64c0c5d. Supports facts: LAM-F-0065, LAM-F-0064. Rights basis: LoC Chronicling America page OUTSIDE the ruled 1933-1939 range: needs the owner to extend the 2026-10-27 ruling to this year (brief lists CA pages generally). Shown only after that. A 1953 item; placed in birth because it gives her birth name and native Vienna (no PD record from 1914 was found). Could move to legacy. Page snapshot snapshots/loc-sn83045462_1953-04-10_ed-1_sp_6.json.\nrights_url set on 2026-10-30 to the page record itself (was https://www.loc.gov/homepage/legal.html, which does not carry the Chronicling America statement; the statement is on the page record, as on the round-7 pages)."
