    {
      "@id": "ihh:LAM-Q-0311",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startedAtTime": "2026-10-29",
      "ihh:family": "round9",
      "instrument": "Chronicling America json + LoC Text Services",
      "query": "louis mayer normandie ; mayer normandie actress (dates 1937-09-15/1937-10-15)",
      "ihh:results": 28,
      "prov:wasAssociatedWith": {
        "@type": "prov:Agent",
        "name": "claude:claude-opus-5-5 (round9 research agent)"
      },
      "ihh:run": {
        "@id": "ihh:run-lamarr-round9-2026-10-29"
      },
      "description": "25 and 3 hits. Read OCR of Evening Star 1937-09-29 p31 (shipping news: NORMANDIE from Havre due), Waterbury Democrat 1937-09-30 p13 (a Normandie arrival naming others), San Antonio Light 1937-10-03 p46, Washington Daily News 1937-09-15 p1, Evening Star 1937-09-28 p37. None names Kiesler, Mandl or Lamarr. Ship and departure port stay single-source (LAM-F-0024, LAM-F-0028)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "ihh:LAM-Q-0312",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startedAtTime": "2026-10-29",
      "ihh:family": "round9",
      "instrument": "WebSearch (allowed_domains si.edu, loc.gov, invent.org, lbi.org, jmw.at, archives.gov, nps.gov, britannica.com)",
      "query": "Hedy Lamarr 1937 fled to London met Louis B. Mayer",
      "ihh:results": 10,
      "prov:wasAssociatedWith": {
        "@type": "prov:Agent",
        "name": "claude:claude-opus-5-5 (round9 research agent)"
      },
      "ihh:run": {
        "@id": "ihh:run-lamarr-round9-2026-10-29"
      },
      "description": "Smithsonian Lemelson Center, 'A Movie Star, Some Player Pianos, and Torpedoes' (invention.si.edu/invention-stories/movie-star-some-player-pianos-and-torpedoes): 'She broke away from Mandl in 1937 and went to England.' curl got HTTP 403; read in a browser. One registered holder only (the National WWII Museum and JWA, both unregistered, say London, not England), so it cannot pass G5; not staged. Jewish Museum Vienna 'Lady Bluetooth' page: 'In 1937 ... she fled to Hollywood' (no England). Britannica answered 403 and its saved snapshot (LAM-S-0010) does not mention England. Lamarr stays pins only: Vienna (birth) and New York (LAM-F-0100)."
    },
